  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats delivered a 97-minute performance at the Majestic Theatre in Detroit on September 29, 2025, captured in a matrix recording that blends soundboard audio with audience microphones [1][2]. This is the 440th show in the archive’s collection for the band, following a previous date at Crusens the day before [2]. The setlist spans their catalog, opening with “New Britain” from *Full Force Galesburg* and “Corsican Mastiff Stride” from *Getting Into Knives* [1]. Notable rare tracks include “Bones Don’t Rust” and “Broken to Begin With,” each with only a handful of archived performances [1][2]. The band played “Weekend in Western Illinois,” a song absent from the archive for over two years, alongside “Un rêve plus long que la nuit,” which had not appeared in nearly seventeen years [2]. Other selections include “Chanson du Bon Chose,” “Great Pirates,” and “Werewolf Gimmick” [1]. The performance concluded with a cover of “Sweet Jane” by The Velvet Underground, a track with only two archived performances, which the uploader noted as a surprising and effective finale [1]. The recording was taped and transferred by Tape&Bake, with thanks extended to Brandon Eggleston and the band’s management for supporting live taping [1].",
